# A346133

Numbers N = A * B such that N (reversed digits) = A (reversed digits) * B (reversed digits). A single-digit number is its own reversal and neither A nor B has a leading zero. No pair (A, B) has both A and B palindromic or simple-digit. The reversed products are not included in the sequence.

The 54 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

